  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71ab8cb112e99c01527b75d950776b833dfac95986abbd891dd054d045712125",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71ab8cb112e9-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, when a district court resolves a purely legal issue at summary judgment, the issue is preserved for appellate review and does not require additional motions at trial."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71ab8cb112e99c01527b75d950776b833dfac95986abbd891dd054d045712125",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71ab8cb112e9-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, parties could preserve purely legal issues by adding one sentence to Rule\u202f50 JMOL motions."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. SAHARIA",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71ab8cb112e99c01527b75d950776b833dfac95986abbd891dd054d045712125",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71ab8cb112e9-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 34,
                "start": 34
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. SAHARIA, when a court denies a defendant\u2019s motion for summary judgment on an affirmative defense, the defendant must raise the defense at trial to preserve it, and must move under Rules\u202f50(a) and (b) to preserve a judgment different from the jury\u2019s verdict."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. SAHARIA",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "71ab8cb112e99c01527b75d950776b833dfac95986abbd891dd054d045712125",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-71ab8cb112e9-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 34,
                "start": 34
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. SAHARIA, if a court denies summary judgment on a question of law, the claim or defense remains live until trial; the only way to finally adjudicate it at summary judgment is to grant summary judgment to one of the parties."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
